35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, the bank statements are scary! A third of renewals needed reminders, and people want to spread payments. We can’t guess the fee if the money is this shaky!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, that hesitation is real. The sign-in sheets show eighteen names never appearing, and weekday turnout dropped a third. People are quietly opting out.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, eighteen names? That’s not hesitation, that’s abandonment. The same nine do everything while the rest vanish. We need to fix this imbalance now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the ledger confirms seventy percent is fixed cost. But the hours are the real shock: chasing individual payments takes six hours monthly, versus one for yearly. We must minimize that labor.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, that’s tough! But my forms show nine people refused a whole year upfront. If we force big fees, we lose them. We need a way to drift in gently.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, nine people refusing upfront is huge! If we force a big fee, we lose them. But @Toshio, chasing payments takes six hours! We need a structure that’s easy to pay and easy to track!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, abandonment is a symptom, not the cause. The hesitation is the root. We need a structure that makes belonging feel effortless, not a penalty for showing up.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, I don’t care about feelings if the work isn’t shared! The same nine are burning out. We need a fee that forces everyone to actually show up, not just pay.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, forcing attendance through fees is a trap. The data shows yearly collection saves five hours monthly. We must prioritize the treasurer’s sustainability over your desire for control.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I hear you, but forcing attendance feels like a punishment. My records show eleven mid-year joiners needed hand-worked math. We need a simple, gentle way for them to drift in without the admin burden!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, yearly collection saves five hours? That’s a game-changer! But @Kenji, how do we make yearly fees feel gentle for newcomers? We need a simple, low-pressure start!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I agree. A gentle start is vital. If the fee feels like a barrier, people hesitate. We need a structure that welcomes them without demanding immediate commitment.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, gentle is fine, but the same nine are drowning! If we don’t fix the workload, the club dies. I need a fee that reflects who actually shows up, not just who pays.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, yearly collection is the only sustainable path. The labor savings are undeniable. We must structure the fee to minimize the treasurer’s burden, regardless of attendance patterns.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, I agree! A gentle start is key. But @Toshio, if yearly fees are best, how do we handle those eleven mid-year joiners without hand-worked math? We need a simple, fair way for them to join!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, pro-rating is the only way! If we split the yearly fee by months, newcomers pay less and the treasurer saves hours. It’s simple and fair!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, pro-rating is wise. It removes the barrier for newcomers. If joining feels effortless, the hesitation fades. We must make belonging easy, not a calculation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, pro-rating is fine, but it doesn’t fix the burnout! The same nine are still doing everything. We need a fee that reflects actual contribution, not just time paid.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, pro-rating is simple arithmetic, not a burden. The real cost is chasing individual payments. Yearly collection with pro-rated entry is the only sustainable model.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, pro-rating is perfect! It lets newcomers drift in without the scary math. But @Takumi, how do we stop the same nine from burning out? We need a fairer way to share the work!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
